    "id": "C1",
    "text": "With add_imports configured, a leading '# isort: skip' import is moved below the sorted import block instead of staying pinned.",
    "source_quote": "With `add_imports` configured, an `# isort: skip` import at the start of a file was moved below the sorted import block and into its own section, instead of keeping the position the directive pins it to.",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "differs"
   },
   {
    "id": "C2",
    "text": "Without add_imports configured, a leading '# isort: skip' import remains in its original position when sorting.",
    "source_quote": "Sorting the same file without `add_imports` left it in place.",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "same"
   },
   {
    "id": "C3",
    "text": "A skipped import at the very start of the import section is collected before any other import sets contains_imports, so the section\u2011boundary guard from #2092 does not apply to it.",
    "source_quote": "A skipped import at the very start of the import section is collected before any other import sets `contains_imports`, so the section-boundary guard added for #2092 never applies to it.",
    "testable": false,
    "expect": "same"
   },
   {
    "id": "C4",
    "text": "When the section is flushed, the configured add_imports are prepended ahead of the collected section, moving the sorted block's insertion point in front of the skipped line and causing output.sorted_imports to splice the sorted imports before it, relocating the skipped import below the block.",
    "source_quote": "When the section is flushed, the configured `add_imports` are prepended ahead of the collected section, which moves the sorted block's insertion point (`parsed.import_index`) in front of the skipped line.",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "differs"
   },
   {
    "id": "C5",
    "text": "In core.process, leading '# isort: skip' lines are kept first when prepending add_imports, so the skipped import stays in place and the added imports are sorted into the block below it.",
    "source_quote": "In `core.process`, keep leading `# isort: skip` lines first when prepending `add_imports`, so the skipped import keeps its position and the added imports are sorted into the block below it.",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "differs"
   }
